      "text": "The application of the Burgers equation in transportation systems has been extensively studied. For instance, Payne (1971, 1979) utilized the Burgers equation to develop mathematical models for traﬃc ﬂow, focusing on the propagation of shock waves and the behavior of traﬃc under varying conditions. These models provided insights into the dynamics of traﬃc congestion and helped improve traﬃc management strategies.",
