        "x1": 0.862523183655433,
        "y1": 0.8929835281854301
      },
      "text": "The Burgers equation’s ability to describe the nonlinear interactions between vehicles and the environment makes it a cornerstone in traﬃc ﬂow theory. By incorporating viscosity and external forcing terms, researchers can model the eﬀects of road conditions, driver behavior, and traﬃc regulations on ﬂow dynamics.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
